WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.650
- China's central bank plans

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.940
to replace its cash with an alternative,

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.490
a digital version of
its national currency.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.370
Think of it like cash
but only on your phone,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.980
a cryptocurrency that's issued

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.610
by the People's Bank of China

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.670
and backed by the renminbi.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.200
- [Narrator] A new global currency.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.240
- After Facebook announced

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.020
the launch of its own cryptocurrency,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.030
the central bank accelerated its work.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.530
China is already well on its way

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.560
to becoming a cashless society.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.650
Over 600 million Chinese,
almost half the country,

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.538
already use apps such as Alibaba's Alipay

00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:33.680
and Tencent's WeChat to pay for everything

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.870
from groceries to bike rentals.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.400
Today the two companies
handle close to 90%

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.440
of China's third party
mobile payments market.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.220
The central bank's currency will provide

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.840
a new payment tool to substitute cash.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.720
Unlike Alipay or WeChat,
users won't be limited

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.740
to paying within one platform.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.870
China plans for its crypto to be accepted

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.190
by any individual or institution,

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.340
just like banknotes and coins.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.440
If Beijing's plan materialize,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.470
China could become the first major nation

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.950
to go completely cash-free
and that could reverberate

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.400
across the global financial system.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.140
- If it succeed, I would
expect that a large number

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.110
of other countries will want
to emulate their success.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.050
- There is still known
about how the system,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.030
known as Digital Currency
Electronic Payments or DCEP

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.620
will operate and what it will look like.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.060
So we examined official
statements and documents

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.210
to understand why China is pushing hard

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.733
into this crypto future.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.720
This is Mu Changchun.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.150
He oversees the central bank's
digital currency efforts

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.830
and is the country's most outspoken

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.420
authority on the rollout.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.220
Since August, he has given a number

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.860
of speeches on China's digital yuan,

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.210
and even launched an online
course about Facebook's Libra

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.258
on a popular Chinese education app.

00:01:48.258 --> 00:01:52.227
(man speaks in foreign language)

00:01:52.227 --> 00:01:54.670
Facebook's plans to provide
its two billion users

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.370
with a brand new digital currency

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.970
spooked central banks around
the world, including China's.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.950
- They see that Libra could be a way

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.440
of extending American financial hegemony

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.180
into the digital currency space as well,

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.540
say, helping to implement
sanctions and export controls.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.820
Beijing historically sought decentralized

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.740
digital currencies like Bitcoin

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.870
as a threat to a long standing pillar

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.730
of its monetary policy capital control.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.970
But then in October,
Chinese president Xi Jinping

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.390
spoke about the important
role of blockchain,

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.090
endorsing the government's embrace

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.900
of the technology that
powers cryptocurrencies.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.380
- They're looking at this and saying,

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.840
is there some element
of it that we'd like.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.940
And actually, what they
found is that blockchain

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.280
is an excellent technology for tracking.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.930
- That could give an
unprecedented level of power

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.310
for any central bank in the
world over capital movements.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.130
Officials say the digital currency

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.610
will not challenge Alipay and WeChat,

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.650
but it would have some similarities.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.850
Like WeChat and Alipay, it
will need a digital wallet.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.930
But unlike the paying platforms,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.480
it won't require a bank account.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.093
Instead, commercial banks will
issue the digital wallets.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.170
A unique aspect of China's crypto

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.670
will be that payments
can be conducted offline.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.390
So in case of a natural disaster

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.020
when the network is down or
if you're onboard a plane,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.820
you can still pay as long
as your phone has power.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.810
And authorities promise a major difference

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.640
will be greater anonymity,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.040
but it won't be absolute anonymity.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.310
This patent filed by
the central bank in 2017

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.900
shows that it's researched
ways to track digital cash.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.480
Marketers won't know what
people spend their money on

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.490
but that information will still be visible

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.450
to the central bank to a certain extent.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.830
- One of the most interesting
aspects of the system

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:42.020
is how much data will
the central bank have

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.960
about where things go 'cause
that's one of the largest,

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.300
most important differences

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.110
between digital currency and cash.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.610
- The central bank calls
this controllable anonymity

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.640
and says big data can help identify

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.210
certain behavioral characteristics.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.180
Officials say tracking transactions

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.950
will help battle money laundering,

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.420
tax evasion, and terrorist financing,

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.660
which is harder to do
with cash transactions.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.900
And while the central
bank says it won't spy

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:11.280
on citizen's everyday transactions,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.800
experts are worried that
China's cryptocurrency

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.380
will allow greater state surveillance.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.000
China's central bank is
not the only one pursuing

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:21.080
a digital state-backed currency,

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.300
but it is likely to be the
first major one to launch it.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.090
Beyond replacing cash, this could

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:28.080
internationalize the renminbi,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.880
and experts think possibly create

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.620
less dependency on the US dollar.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.670
There's still a long
way before that happens.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.600
Though most governments are
still weary about crypto,

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.483
the world will be watching
China's experiment closely.

